\details{
Implements parametric and semiparametric likelihood ratio procedures for
comparing two groups when an endpoint comprises a substantive atom and a
continuous non-atom outcome.

The package is organized around a standardized internal data representation
with columns \code{Y}, \code{A}, and \code{R}, optionally augmented with baseline covariates
supplied through \code{adjust}.

Exported user-facing helpers include:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=trunc_comp]{trunc_comp()}} for fitting the model.
\item \code{\link[=trunc_comp_bayes]{trunc_comp_bayes()}} for the experimental Bayesian pathway.
\item \code{\link[=posterior_density_plot]{posterior_density_plot()}} for plotting the arm-specific posterior outcome
densities implied by the Bayesian fit.
\item \code{\link[=posterior_predictive_check]{posterior_predictive_check()}} for \code{bayesplot}-based posterior predictive
checks of the Bayesian fit.
\item \code{\link[=posterior_predictive_pvalues]{posterior_predictive_pvalues()}} for discrepancy-based posterior
predictive p values from the Bayesian fit.
\item \code{\link[=summary.trunc_comp_fit]{summary.trunc_comp_fit()}} and \code{\link[=print.trunc_comp_fit]{print.trunc_comp_fit()}} for displaying results.
\item \code{\link[=summary.trunc_comp_bayes_fit]{summary.trunc_comp_bayes_fit()}} and \code{\link[=print.trunc_comp_bayes_fit]{print.trunc_comp_bayes_fit()}} for
Bayesian posterior summaries.
\item \code{\link[=confint.trunc_comp_fit]{confint.trunc_comp_fit()}} and \code{\link[=joint_contrast_surface]{joint_contrast_surface()}} for marginal and
joint inference.
\item \code{\link[=simulate_truncated_data]{simulate_truncated_data()}}, \code{trunc_comp_example}, and
\code{trunc_comp_adjusted_example} for reproducible examples.
}

For successful unadjusted fits the package stores the coded endpoint mean
difference \code{delta}. Confidence intervals for \code{delta} are
computed on demand through \code{\link[=confint.trunc_comp_fit]{confint.trunc_comp_fit()}} using
\code{method = "welch"}, \code{"profile"}, or \code{"projected"}.

Adjusted fits return conditional treatment contrasts from the fitted
regression components. Their joint component confidence region profiles the
adjustment coefficients. Because those coefficients do not define a marginal
coded endpoint contrast without a standardization target, \code{delta} and its
intervals are unavailable for adjusted fits.
